.TH SHIKI 1 2026-10-04 "shiki 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shiki \- drive Shikidan from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shiki
.I command
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-url
.IR URL ]
.br
.B shiki
.RI [ command ]
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shiki
talks to a running Shikidan server over its HTTP API. It covers the
everyday work of the cockpit without a browser: checking status and usage,
starting and following jobs, answering permission requests, running Studio
workflows, and managing terminals.
.PP
Every command prints short human\-readable output by default. With
.B \-\-json
it prints the server's JSON response unchanged, which is the form scripts and
AI agents should read.
.PP
Shikidan must be running (start it with
.B bun run start
in the repository).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
Shikidan server address. Default:
.BR $SKD_URL ,
then
.BR http://127.0.0.1:7777 .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the server JSON as one document on stdout. For
.B job follow
and
.BR "job new \-\-follow" ,
print NDJSON instead (one JSON object per line, see
.BR "JSON OUTPUT" ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help for
.B shiki
or for one command group, for example
.BR "shiki job \-\-help" .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print
.B shiki
and its version, then exit 0. Works after any command too.
.PP
Running
.B shiki
with no arguments prints the Shikidan banner, the version and the
command list.
.B \-\-help
prints the command list without the banner, so scripts can read it.
.PP
Unknown options are a usage error.
.SH STATUS AND SETTINGS
.TP
.B shiki status
Whether Shikidan is up, usage per provider (5\-hour, weekly or monthly
window), which engine and model play each role, and the fallback AI.
.TP
.B shiki roles
Show the engine and model for each role, and the fallback AI that steps
use when their role is not defined or their AI cannot start.
.TP
.BI "shiki roles set " "role connection" " \fR[\fB\-\-model\fR \fIM\fR]"
Give
.I role
to a built\-in AI
.RB ( claude ,
.BR glm ,
.BR codex )
or a connection id from
.BR "shiki connections" ,
and optionally a model.
An AI that is not connected is refused before anything is saved.
.I role
is
.BR plan ,
.BR execute ,
.B review
or a named role of letters, digits,
.B \-
and
.B _
that flow steps can ask for.
The other roles and the fallback keep their current values.
.TP
.B shiki models
Models each engine offers.
.TP
.B shiki providers
Connected AI providers.
.TP
.B shiki connections
Built\-in and connected AI agents.
.TP
.BI "shiki connection add " preset " \fR[\fB\-\-id\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-command\fR \fICMD\fR] [\fB\-\-arg\fR \fIARG\fR]... [\fB\-\-model\fR \fIM\fR]... [\fB\-\-probe\fR]"
Connect an AI from a preset:
.BR grok ,
.BR qwen ,
.BR opencode ,
.B custom\-agent
or
.BR custom\-cli .
The id defaults to the preset name and must not exist yet.
.B \-\-command
replaces the preset's command,
.B \-\-arg
its arguments and
.B \-\-model
its model list; repeat the last two for more.
The preset's model family comes along, so cross\-family review knows a
.B grok
connection is not Claude.
.B \-\-probe
checks the connection after saving (not for CLI connections).
.TP
.BI "shiki connection set " id " \fR[\fB\-\-command\fR \fICMD\fR] [\fB\-\-arg\fR \fIARG\fR]... [\fB\-\-model\fR \fIM\fR]... [\fB\-\-probe\fR]"
Change a connected AI.
Each option given replaces that part of the saved connection; the rest is kept.
.TP
.BI "shiki connection remove " id
Remove a connected AI.
Refused while a role or the fallback uses it; move the role first with
.BR "shiki roles set" .
.TP
.BI "shiki connection probe " id
Ask a connected agent what it can do.
.TP
.BI "shiki connection models " id " \fR[\fB\-\-refresh\fR]"
The models a connected agent offers: what it reported first, then any extra IDs from its settings,
when they were last checked, and the last error.
Shikidan re-checks a day after a success and 15 minutes after a failure, whenever the list is read.
CLI connections cannot report models; list them in the connection's settings.
With
.BR \-\-json ,
prints the saved check result.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Ask the agent for its models now and print what it found.
.RE
.TP
.B shiki flow\-approval
Whether flows started by an AI wait for your approval.
.TP
.BI "shiki flow\-approval set " value
Turn flow approval
.B on
or
.BR off
.RB ( true " and " false
also work).
.TP
.B shiki notify status
The webhook url, whether a key is set, how many events still wait to be delivered,
and how many were dropped because more than 200 were waiting (the oldest go first).
.TP
.B shiki notify test
Send a sample event to the webhook now and print the HTTP status it answered.
The sample carries real\-sized images (the renders of your latest queue item with a pick, or three 800 KB blobs), so a size limit on the receiving side shows up at once.
.TP
.BI "shiki notify set\-url " url
Set the webhook url. It must be https.
Shikidan POSTs a JSON event to it whenever a queue card needs a person
(a pick, a question, a failure, a stage or a landing), a run is blocked, or a
job asks for permission or runs slow.
.TP
.BI "shiki notify set\-key " key
Set the shared key sent as
.B Authorization: Bearer
and
.BR X\-Automation\-Key .
Pass
.B \-
to read it from stdin and keep it out of shell history.
.TP
.B shiki notify clear
Remove the url and key. Events still waiting to be delivered are dropped.
.TP
.B shiki policy
The policy template every workflow step receives.
.SH WAITING ON YOU
.TP
.B shiki attention
Everything waiting on you: permission requests, finished or stuck jobs, runs
waiting for approval. Permission requests show the request id that
.B job permission
needs.
.TP
.BI "shiki attention dismiss " key
Dismiss one waiting item. Permission requests cannot be dismissed; answer them
with
.BR "job permission" .
.SH HISTORY
.TP
.BI "shiki history " \fR[\fB\-\-limit\fR " N\fR]"
Recent chats, jobs, terminals and sessions.
.B \-\-limit
shows only the first
.I N
items.
.TP
.B shiki outcomes \-\-chat \fIID\fR | \-\-terminal \fIID\fR [\-\-after \fIN\fR] [\-\-limit \fIN\fR]
Outcome ledger of one chat or terminal. Exactly one of
.B \-\-chat
or
.B \-\-terminal
is required.
.B \-\-after
skips the first
.I N
outcomes;
.B \-\-limit
returns at most
.IR N .
.SH JOBS AND CHATS
A job is one AI run: a chat turn, a dispatched task, or a workflow step.
.TP
.B shiki jobs \fR[\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-chat\fR \fIID\fR]
List jobs, newest first: id, status, engine, age and the first line of the
prompt.
.B \-\-limit
keeps the newest
.IR N ;
.B \-\-chat
keeps only jobs of that chat.
.TP
.BI "shiki job new " prompt " \fR[\fIoptions\fR]"
Start a job. Pass
.B \-
as the prompt to read it from stdin.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-engine " E"
Engine to run. Default:
.BR claude .
.TP
.BI \-\-model " M"
Model id.
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd " DIR"
Repository to work in. Default: the current folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-label " L"
Job name. Default: the first line of the prompt, cut to 60 characters.
.TP
.B \-\-worktree
Run in an isolated git worktree.
.TP
.B \-\-follow
Stream the output until the job ends, then exit as
.B job follow
does.
.RE
.TP
.BI "shiki job show " id
One job with its recent activity.
.TP
.BI "shiki job log " id
The full job log as raw text.
.TP
.BI "shiki job follow " id
Stream a job until it ends. Exits 0 if the job finished, 1 if it failed or was
killed. Following an existing job starts from roughly the last 4 KB of its log.
In human mode the engine's raw output is printed as it arrives; for Claude and
Codex that is JSON event lines.
.TP
.BI "shiki job reply " "id text"
Send a follow\-up message to a job. Pass
.B \-
as the text to read it from stdin.
.TP
.BI "shiki job permission " "id decision" " \-\-request " RID
Answer a permission request.
.I decision
is
.BR allow_once ,
.B allow_always
or
.BR deny .
.B \-\-request
is required; find the id with
.BR "shiki attention" .
.TP
.BI "shiki job kill " id
Stop a running job.
.TP
.BI "shiki job land " id
Land a job's worktree changes on its branch.
.TP
.BI "shiki job reviewed " id
Mark a job as reviewed.
.TP
.BI "shiki job undo " "id toolUseId"
Undo one Edit or MultiEdit tool call of a chat turn.
.TP
.BI "shiki job rename " "id label" " \fR[\fB\-\-lock\fR]"
Rename a chat.
.B \-\-lock
stops automatic retitling. Works on chat roots only.
.TP
.BI "shiki job export " id " \fR[\fB\-\-leaf\fR \fITURN\fR]"
Export a chat as markdown.
.B \-\-leaf
picks which branch of the conversation to export.
.TP
.BI "shiki job thread " id " \fR[\fB\-\-leaf\fR \fITURN\fR]"
Messages of a job's thread.
.TP
.BI "shiki job commands " id
Slash commands the job's engine offers.
.TP
.BI "shiki job queue " id
Messages queued behind a running reply.
.TP
.BI "shiki job queue rm " "id itemId"
Remove one queued message.
.SH STUDIO WORKFLOWS AND RUNS
.TP
.B shiki workflows
Saved workflows; the default is marked with
.BR * .
.TP
.BI "shiki workflow revisions " id
Revision history of one workflow.
.TP
.B shiki runs \fR[\fB\-\-chat\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-terminal\fR \fIID\fR]
Workflow runs, optionally only those of one chat or terminal.
.TP
.BI "shiki run show " id
One run in full.
.TP
.BI "shiki run start " "workflowId request" " \fR[\fIoptions\fR]"
Start a workflow run. Pass
.B \-
as the request to read it from stdin.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-label " L"
Run name. Default: the first line of the request, cut to 120 characters.
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd " DIR"
Repository to work in. Default: the current folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-revision " REV"
Workflow revision. Default: latest.
.TP
.BI \-\-engine " E" "\fR, " \-\-model " M"
Engine and model override.
.TP
.BI \-\-terminal " ID" "\fR, " \-\-chat " ID"
Terminal or chat that owns the run.
.RE
.TP
.BI "shiki run stop " id
Stop a run.
.TP
.BI "shiki run retry " id
Retry a run's failed step.
.TP
.BI "shiki run pause " id
Pause a run.
.TP
.BI "shiki run resume " id
Resume a paused run.
.TP
.BI "shiki run approve " id " \fR[\fIsession options\fR]"
Approve a run waiting for you.
.TP
.BI "shiki run reject " id " \fR[\fIsession options\fR]"
Reject a run waiting for you.
.TP
.BI "shiki run changes " id " \-\-graph " FILE " \-\-reason " TEXT " \fR[\fB\-\-scope\-grew\fR] [\fIsession options\fR]"
Propose a change to a running flow.
.B \-\-graph
is a JSON file with the proposed graph.
.B \-\-scope\-grew
marks a change that widens the scope.
.TP
.BI "shiki run step " "runId nodeId" " \fR[\fIsession options\fR]"
Read a step waiting on this session.
.TP
.BI "shiki run step " "runId nodeId" " \-\-post \-\-outcome " O " \-\-summary " TEXT " \fR[\fB\-\-evidence\fR \fITEXT\fR]... [\fB\-\-output\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fIsession options\fR]"
Report a step result.
.I O
is
.BR pass ,
.B fail
or
.BR blocked .
Repeat
.B \-\-evidence
for each piece of evidence.
.TP
.BI "shiki run remind " "runId nodeId"
Remind the session about a waiting step. The server only accepts this from the
browser, so from
.B shiki
it fails with exit status 1.
.PP
.I Session options
identify who is answering:
.BI \-\-chat " ID" ,
.BI \-\-terminal " ID"
(the chat or terminal that owns the run) and
.BI \-\-flow\-version " N"
(the whole\-number version being answered).
.SH TERMINALS
.TP
.B shiki terminals
Live terminals: id, engine, age, title and folder.
.TP
.BR "shiki terminal new " [ \fIoptions\fR ]
Open a new terminal.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-engine " E"
Engine to run. Default:
.BR claude .
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd " DIR"
Folder to open in. Default: the current folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " M" "\fR, " \-\-title " T"
Model id and terminal name.
.TP
.BI \-\-resume " SID"
Session id to resume.
.TP
.BI \-\-workflow " ID" "\fR, " \-\-revision " REV"
Pin a workflow (and revision) to the terminal.
.RE
.TP
.BI "shiki terminal rename " "id name"
Rename a terminal.
.TP
.BI "shiki terminal close " id
End a terminal.
.TP
.BI "shiki terminal thread " id
Transcript of a terminal session.
.TP
.BR "shiki terminal sessions " [ \-\-cwd \fI\ DIR\fR ]
Past sessions a terminal could resume in a folder. Default: the current folder.
.SH PLUGINS AND MARKETPLACES
Plugins are installed from git and listed by marketplaces. Isolated plugins run
under the OS sandbox; trusted plugins get full access.
.TP
.B shiki plugin list
Installed plugins: id, version, runtime, state and name.
.TP
.B shiki plugin catalog \fR[\fB\-\-refresh\fR]
Plugins your marketplaces offer, and any marketplace that failed to load.
.B \-\-refresh
fetches every marketplace first.
.TP
.BI "shiki plugin add " link " \fR[\fB\-\-ref\fR \fIREF\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-trust\fR]"
A plugin link shows what the plugin asks for; add
.B \-\-yes
to install it (and
.B \-\-trust
for a trusted plugin). A marketplace link is added. Without
.B \-\-ref
the newest version tag is used, or the default branch.
.TP
.BI "shiki plugin update " id " \fR[\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-accept\fR] [\fB\-\-trust\fR]"
Check for a newer version (re\-reading its marketplace first) and, with
.BR \-\-yes ,
apply it. An update that asks for more needs
.BR \-\-accept ;
one that becomes trusted needs
.BR \-\-trust .
.TP
.BI "shiki plugin remove " id " \fR[\fB\-\-delete\-data\fR]"
Uninstall; its settings and files are kept unless
.BR \-\-delete\-data .
.TP
.BI "shiki plugin enable " id ", shiki plugin disable " id
Turn a plugin on or off.
.TP
.BI "shiki plugin settings " id
Its settings; secrets show only whether they are set.
.TP
.BI "shiki plugin set " "id key value" ", shiki plugin unset " "id key"
Change a declared setting. A value of
.B \-
is read from stdin, which keeps tokens out of shell history.
An on/off setting takes
.B true
or
.BR false .
.TP
.BI "shiki plugin call " "id method" " \fR[\fB\-\-params\fR \fIJSON\fR|\fB\-\fR]"
Call one of the plugin's own server methods and print its result.
.TP
.BI "shiki marketplace list\fR, \fBshiki marketplace add " url "\fR, \fBshiki marketplace remove " url
Manage marketplaces directly;
.B add
on an existing one refreshes it.
.SH CLICKUP BOARD
Commands for the ClickUp board plugin (clickup\-board). A board is named by its
id or its name.
.TP
.BI "shiki clickup connect " token
Save your ClickUp personal token
.RB ( \- " reads stdin)"
and check it.
.TP
.B shiki clickup boards
Saved boards with their filter count and folder.
.TP
.BI "shiki clickup board " board " \fR[\fB\-\-search\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR]"
The board as the screen shows it, with its saved filters applied: tasks per
status and how many of the total are shown.
.B \-\-all
ignores the saved filters.
.TP
.B shiki clickup board add \fR(\fB\-\-link\fR \fIURL\fR | \fB\-\-list\fR \fIID\fR) \fB\-\-folder\fR \fIDIR\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR]
Save a board from a ClickUp list or board view link, or a list id.
.TP
.BI "shiki clickup board remove " board
Remove a saved board.
.TP
.B shiki clickup tree \fR[\fB\-\-team\fR|\fB\-\-space\fR|\fB\-\-folder\fR \fIID\fR]
Browse workspaces, spaces, folders and lists to find a list id.
.TP
.BI "shiki clickup filters " board " \fR[\fB\-\-fields\fR]"
The board's filters, numbered; the ClickUp view's own filter is marked
.BR (view) .
.B \-\-fields
lists every field and its operators.
.TP
.BI "shiki clickup filter add " "board field operator" " \fR[\fB\-\-value\fR \fIV\fR]..."
Add a filter. Fields, operators and values are matched by name, as in the
screen, for example
.B Assignee \(dqis any of\(dq \-\-value Me
or
.BR "Planning is \-\-value \(dqSprint 17\(dq" .
Dates for Before and After are YYYY\-MM\-DD.
.TP
.BI "shiki clickup filter remove " "board N" "\fR, \fBshiki clickup filter clear " board "\fR, \fBshiki clickup filter join " "board " and|or
Remove filter N, remove all of them (the view's own stay), or combine them
with AND or OR.
.TP
.BI "shiki clickup task " id
Print the task dossier the AI reads first.
.TP
.BI "shiki clickup start " id " \fR[\fIoptions\fR]"
Write the task dossier into the session folder and start a chat (or with
.B \-\-terminal
a terminal) that reads it first. The folder is
.BR \-\-cwd ,
else the
.B \-\-board
folder, else the current one; the AI is
.BR \-\-engine ,
else the plan role. Also
.BR \-\-model " and " \-\-message .
.SH QUEUE
The build queue builds source items (such as ClickUp tasks) in order, one at a
time unless
.B shiki queue parallel
raises it. An item
that needs answers waits and resumes when the source replies. When a run stops
because no AI can start (missing token, CLI not installed, usage limit
reached), its item goes back first in line and the queue pauses until the
usage limit resets, or for 5, then 15, then 60 minutes, and then resumes by
itself.
.TP
.B shiki queue list
Items in build order: id, state, source, title, and the error or open
questions.
Every command that takes an item
.I id
also accepts the start of an id: at least 4 characters that match exactly one item.
An id that matches several items is refused.
.TP
.BI "shiki queue add " "source externalId" " \fR[\fB\-\-repo\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-flow\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-next\fR]"
Add an item. It is built in
.B \-\-repo
(default: the current folder) with the saved flow
.BR \-\-flow ;
.B \-\-next
puts it first.
.TP
.BI "shiki queue move " "id to"
Move an item to position
.I to
(0 is first).
.TP
.BI "shiki queue parallel " n
Build up to
.I n
cards at once, 1 to 4 (default 1). Keep 1 for projects whose worktrees share
one test database: two cards running tests at once deadlock there.
.TP
.BI "shiki queue poll " minutes
Check ClickUp for replies to questions and design picks every
.I minutes
minutes, 1 to 15 (default 2). The new pace applies straight away.
.TP
.BI "shiki queue publish\-days " n
Take published mockups down after
.I n
days, 1 to 90 (default 14). They also come down when the card lands or is
removed.
.TP
.BI "shiki queue ask\-to " "\fR[\fIuserId\fR | \fB\-\-clear\fR]"
Ask design picks to the ClickUp user with this id (digits, up to 30) instead
of the card's owner: they are tagged and assigned, and their replies decide
the pick. With
.B \-\-clear
the card's owner is asked again (the default); with no argument it prints the
current setting. It applies to asks posted from now on.
.TP
.BI "shiki queue none\-phrases " "\fR[\fIphrase\fR...] [\fB\-\-clear\fR]"
Replace the extra phrases that read as "none of these" in a ClickUp pick reply
(up to 30 phrases of 3 to 60 characters). They are matched like the built-in
ones: case-insensitive, on the first non-empty line, and the rest of the reply
becomes the feedback. With
.B \-\-clear
the list is emptied; with no argument it prints the list.
.TP
.BI "shiki queue unpublish " id
Take down an item's published mockups now.
.TP
.BI "shiki queue requeue " id
Put a failed, ready or waiting item back in line.
A failed item resumes the run it failed in, keeping the steps that passed;
.B \-\-fresh
starts a new run instead.
.TP
.BI "shiki queue pick " "id option"
Choose a design variant for an item waiting on a pick.
.B \-\-tester
names who to tag and
.B \-\-note
adds a note for the next run.
Choose
.B none
with
.BI \-\-feedback " TEXT"
to say what should change; the queue then builds new variants from it.
When the flow's plugin has its
.B autoPick
setting on, the queue takes the recommended variant itself, alerts
.RI "Auto-picked " option
and keeps building; a pick with no recommended variant still waits for you.
A ClickUp reply that is not understood is never dropped silently: the item
shows up in
.B shiki attention
with the reply text and one
.B pick\-unclear
webhook event is sent, so an operator can answer with
.B shiki queue say
and decide with
.B shiki queue pick.
The plugin's
.B automate
setting is one switch. Off, the default (legacy), keeps the pick in
Shikidan and leaves the ClickUp status alone until the UAT stage posts it.
On (full automate) also moves the ClickUp status at every step, from the
flow's
.B sourceStatus
map.
When the flow's plugin has its
.B automate
setting on (full automate,
.IR "shiki plugin set fixstack automate true" ),
the card's mockups are published at
.IB card \- random . domain
(the domain is
.BR SKD_PUBLISH_DOMAIN ,
default
.BR shikidan.com )
and the card owner is tagged in ClickUp with the link. Folders named
.B renders/
or
.B verify/
are never published, and every file under
.BR shots/ ,
or any image with the same bytes as an image downloaded from the card, is
replaced by a placeholder. Only the first line of the owner's reply decides:
.IR "แบบ C" ,
.I "C ครับ"
or
.I "ไม่ชอบเลย อยากได้แบบเดิม"
is taken as the pick, and lines after the option, such as
.I "ปุ่มใหญ่ขึ้นหน่อย"
on the next line, become its note. A first line with anything else on it,
such as
.IR "C ครับ ปุ่มใหญ่ขึ้นหน่อย" ,
leaves the card waiting. The pick is confirmed in ClickUp and the ask comment
is resolved, also when the pick is made here, or the card is requeued or
removed. When publishing or tagging fails, or Shikidan restarted while the
question was being posted, the card waits for a pick here.
.TP
.BI "shiki queue say " "id text"
Write a message for the card's ClickUp owner. While a design pick is open it
goes inside the ask's thread; otherwise it is an update on the card. The
reply cursor does not move, so the message is never read back as a reply.
.TP
.BI "shiki queue reread " id
For an item waiting on a ClickUp pick: read the replies again from the ask
(not from where the last check stopped) and judge them now. Use it after a
reply was read as unclear and you changed what counts as one.
.TP
.BI "shiki queue remove " id
Remove an item that is not building.
.TP
.B shiki queue check
Check sources for replies now instead of waiting for the next check.
.SH JUST FOR FUN
.TP
.B shiki badapple
Play Bad Apple!! as sakura ASCII art in this terminal, sized to fit the
window, with petals drifting over it. Ctrl\-C stops it and restores the
cursor. Sending \fBbadapple\fR on its own in the chat plays it there too.
The silent frames live in \fIpublic/badapple.bin\fR; rebuild them from a
video with \fBbun scripts/badapple.ts\fR \fIvideo\fR.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
With
.BR \-\-json ,
each command prints exactly one JSON document: the server's response. A few
commands wrap text so the output is still JSON:
.TP
.B job log
.B {"log": "..."}
.TP
.B job export
.B {"markdown": "..."}
.TP
.B status
.B {"health": ..., "quota": ..., "roles": ...}
.PP
.B job follow
and
.B job new \-\-follow
print NDJSON: one
.B {"type":"job",...}
line, one
.B {"type":"data","data":...}
line per streamed payload, and a final
.B {"type":"end","status":"..."}
line.
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-limit ,
list commands print the server response unchanged; with it, the list is cut in
.BR shiki .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SKD_URL
Server address when
.B \-\-url
is not given.
.TP
.B SKD_TOKEN
API token sent as
.BR "Authorization: Bearer" .
Default: the
.B apiToken
field of
.B secrets.json
in the Shikidan config folder. Only needed for non\-local addresses;
requests to 127.0.0.1 or localhost need no token. Over a token, only the job,
Studio run and read\-only status routes are reachable.
.TP
.B SKD_CONFIG_DIR
Config folder that holds
.BR secrets.json .
Default:
.BR ~/.config/shikidan .
.TP
.B SKD_PUBLISH_DIR
For
.B bun static\-host/serve.ts
only: the folder it serves. Default:
.BR ~/.config/shikidan/published .
.TP
.B SKD_STATIC_PORT
For
.B static\-host/serve.ts
only: the port it binds on 127.0.0.1. Default: 7780.
.TP
.B SKD_PUBLISH_DOMAIN
The domain design\-pick mockups are published under, read by both the server
(for the link in the ClickUp ask) and
.B static\-host/serve.ts
(for the subdomains it answers), so set it the same for both. Default:
.BR shikidan.com .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. For
.BR "job follow" ,
the job finished.
.TP
.B 1
The server returned an error (its message is printed on stderr), or a followed
job failed or was killed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown command or option, missing argument, invalid value.
.TP
.B 3
Shikidan is not reachable at the URL.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check that everything is up:
.PP
.RS
.B shiki status
.RE
.PP
Start a job with GLM in the current repository and watch it:
.PP
.RS
.B shiki job new """fix the login bug""" \-\-engine glm \-\-follow
.RE
.PP
Pipe a long prompt from a file:
.PP
.RS
.B shiki job new \- \-\-label refactor < prompt.md
.RE
.PP
See what is waiting, then allow a request once:
.PP
.RS
.B shiki attention
.br
.B shiki job permission 32a1609e allow_once \-\-request req_123
.RE
.PP
Start the default workflow and list its runs:
.PP
.RS
.B shiki run start default """build the export page"""
.br
.B shiki runs
.RE
.PP
From a script or AI agent, get the newest five jobs as JSON:
.PP
.RS
.B shiki jobs \-\-limit 5 \-\-json
.RE
.PP
Install ClickUp board and work a task from the shell:
.PP
.RS
.nf
shiki plugin add https://github.com/LynchzDEV/skd\-plugin\-clickup \-\-yes
shiki clickup connect \- < token.txt
shiki clickup filter add main Assignee "is any of" \-\-value Me
shiki clickup board main
shiki clickup start 86d4ccpu2 \-\-board main
.fi
.RE
.SH NOT COVERED
Use the browser for: revealing or rotating the API token and writing the z.ai
token; adding or deleting connections; workflow drafts, previews and editing; the Studio default
workflow; chat home and file pickers; job images; terminal file drops; live
event streams; attaching to a terminal interactively.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/shikidan/secrets.json
Holds the API token used for non\-local servers, the z.ai token and the webhook url and key.
.TP
.B ~/.config/shikidan/notify\-outbox.json
Webhook events not yet delivered, and the last event sent per queue item or job.
Delivery retries after 10 s, 1 min, 5 min, then every 30 min with the same
eventId until the receiver answers 2xx, and resumes after a restart.
.TP
.B ~/.config/shikidan/published/
One folder per card with published design\-pick mockups, named after the
card's subdomain. The separate process
.B bun static\-host/serve.ts
serves it on 127.0.0.1:7780, by Host header only, GET and HEAD only, and
nothing else; put a tunnel in front of that port, never in front of 7777.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shiki " \-\-help" ,
the "Command line" section of the Shikidan README.
